    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1282">

                <pb facs="1239" n="1073" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1073"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115R39/34</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-12T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 12, 1917, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>177. Your telegram 138, April 27, 4 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1282-f1"/> Consul,
                    Nogales, reports Governor, Sonora, unyielding in matter Richardson Company
                    tax.</p>
                <p>Please endeavor obtain from Mexican Government statement regarding results of
                    instructions which Foreign Office promised would be sent to Sonora authorities.
                    Telegraph report.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
